spans.s:
tāḍa,
(1) m. or nt. (Skt. tāla, Pali tāḷa, cymbal or some percussion instrument; also clap of the hand etc.), a musical instrument, cymbal: vīṇāś ca tāḍā paṇavāś ca SP 〔51.13〕 (vs); saṃgīti-tāḍa-samaye ca viniścayajñāḥ RP 〔42.17〕 (vs), but here and in the next tāḍa could mean not the instrument, but the sound made by striking it; vādyatāḍa-nināda-nirghoṣa-śabdair SP 〔338.11〕 (prose); others, see s.v. śamya; see also tāḍāvacara;
(2) m. (= Pali tāḷa, m.; see next), key (in Skt. tāla, lock, cf. tālaka; see Johnston, note on Buddhac.): saddharma-tāḍena Buddhac. 〔1.74〕; tāḍam ādāya gṛham asya gatvā Av 〔ii.56.2〕; tāḍam apahṛtya gṛhaṃ gatvā 3 (ms. tāḍan both times).
